# The Village of Barovia's few people out by day (lane 4, F2): Goodwife Petra carrying water from the well. She walks
# her route (the location's `path`) and is indoors long before dark. Lane 28 (2026-10-08) added Grigore hauling his
# firewood in from the west road and Widow Ileana at her husband's grave.

~ goodwife
if flag.burgomaster_buried
Goodwife Petra: They say the old burgomaster's in the ground at last. Good. A man shouldn't lie in his own parlour waiting for the priest.
-> END
endif
Goodwife Petra [afraid]: Strangers. Don't stand so close to the well. Folk will think you've come to poison it, and then they'll think it's my fault for talking to you.
* Who would poison a well? -> poison
* We'll leave you be. -> END

~ poison
Goodwife Petra: Nobody. That's the point. There's nothing left here worth the trouble. Only the water, and the walk to it, and being home before the light goes.
-> END

~ woodcutter
Grigore: Out of the road, out of the road. This load won't carry itself, and the light won't wait for it.
* Why the hurry? -> woodcutter_hurry
* Sorry. -> END

~ woodcutter_hurry
Grigore: The trees by the west road, you cut what you need by noon and you go. After noon they're not the same trees. Ask anyone who stayed to cut a bit more.
Grigore: Nobody? No. That's my point.
-> END

~ widow
if flag.burgomaster_buried
Widow Ileana: The burgomaster has a proper grave now, over there. My Teodor will be glad of the company. He never liked him, mind.
-> END
endif
Widow Ileana: I'm telling him the news. There's never any news. He doesn't mind; he was always a good listener, and now he's a better one.
* Who was he? -> widow_who
* We'll leave you to it. -> END

~ widow_who
Widow Ileana: Teodor. A cooper. He went to fetch a barrel from the crossroads one evening and came back the next morning, quite well, only very pale and very polite. Father Donavich made me shut the door on him.
Widow Ileana: I did. I still don't know if I was right.
-> END

~ gravedigger
Old Mihail: Mind the edge. It's deeper than it looks. They all are, now. Six feet was enough once. Six feet isn't enough any more.
* Who is it for? -> gravedigger_who
* Why so deep? -> gravedigger_deep
* Goodbye. -> END

~ gravedigger_who
Old Mihail: Nobody yet. There's always somebody by the end of the week. I like to be ready. It's rude to keep them waiting.
-> END

~ gravedigger_deep
Old Mihail: So they stay down. Some of them try to come home, see. Not the ones I've buried. Not yet. I dig deep and I pack it hard.
-> END

~ acolyte
Anca: Good morning. Father Donavich says a swept path is a prayer you can walk on. I sweep it twice, to be sure.
if flag.burgomaster_buried
Anca: It's quieter under the floor since the burial. I sleep better. Father doesn't.
-> END
endif
* What's under the floor? -> acolyte_floor
* Goodbye. -> END

~ acolyte_floor
Anca: Nothing. The cellar. Father says it's the wind in the cellar. The wind says his name, sometimes, and asks for him.
Anca: I sweep a bit louder when it does.
-> END

~ vasile
Vasile: You heard about the burgomaster? Dead. Heart gave out. The wolves stood round the house all night like mourners.
Petre: It wasn't his heart.
Vasile: It was his heart, Petre. Something took it.
-> END

~ petre
Petre: Strangers. Haven't had strangers since the last strangers. They didn't stay long either. Nobody does, except us.
Vasile: We'd leave if we could. Road's open. You just come back round to the gate.
Petre: In the mist. Every time.
-> END

~ goat
Narrator: The goat looks up from the fence it is eating, considers you, and goes back to the fence. It has seen worse than you, and it has eaten better fences.
-> END

